  "title": "Nigerian Civil War (Biafran War)",
  "summary": "After a coup, anti-Igbo killings and failed talks, Nigeria's Eastern Region declared itself the Republic of Biafra on 30 May 1967, and the federal government went to war. A blockade cut Biafra off and caused severe famine. Biafra surrendered in January 1970 and rejoined Nigeria. Estimates of civilian deaths vary widely.",
